From d148fa6d27fd1a9482128f512dde4ed7dcb38985 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite Auditor <auditor@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:14:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] G4 update: ACPI identity pairing, COMPAT plan and doc
 corrections

COMPAT G4.  The machine advertised the Q35 host bridge 8086:29c0 and
implemented its seven PAM bytes, but the LPC function at 0:31.0 reported
Panther Point 8086:1e55 -- the ID the bundled sample firmware knows.  G3
measured that SeaBIOS rel-1.16.3 acpi_setup() recognizes only PIIX4
8086:7113 or ICH9 LPC 8086:2918, so a stock BIOS completed POST and
published no RSDP at all.

--lpc=ich9 (machine_t.cfg_lpc_ich9, src/devices.c) reports 8086:2918, the
identity that pairs with the advertised host bridge; the default keeps
8086:1e55 so every historical lane stays byte-identical.

Measured with the UNMODIFIED diagnostic SeaBIOS bundled in
docs/evidence/compat-g3/ and a blank USB image, --platform=haswell,
--max-instr=200000000, exit 0:
  ACPI DSDT=0x07ffe4b0
  Copying ACPI RSDP from 0x00006dfc to 0x000f6210
and an end-of-run v2-snapshot walk finds a checksum-valid rev-0 RSDP at
0xf6210 -> RSDT 0x7ffe470 (52 B, 4 entries) -> FACP 0x7ffff80 (116 B),
SSDT 0x7fff720 (2073 B), APIC/MADT 0x7fff630 (110 B, LAPIC base
0xfee00000), MCFG 0x7fff5f0 (60 B); every checksum sums to zero.
Negative control: the same ROM under the default identity publishes
NO RSDP.  Control: the G3 probe ROM (which adds 1e55 to the match table)
yields RSDP 0xf6210 with a 3-entry RSDT at 0x7ffe4c0 and no MCFG -- the
extra MCFG is the receipt that the ICH9 identity unlocks SeaBIOS's full
Q35/PCIe path, not merely the old match table.

tests/test_compat.c pins 7 vectors: both identities, class 06/01 and the
multifunction header, the untouched host bridge and AHCI function, and
Q35 PAM under the ICH9 identity.  make test-compat is wired into
make test and make test-sanitize; both full gates pass (368 ok lines,
RC 0 each).  The bundled sample firmware under the flag is unchanged:
HALTED, executed=4837677, GUEST_OK, framebuffer marker 0x00200000.

Docs and hygiene:
  - docs/plans/COMPAT_PLAN.md: the missing G0-G6 plan, in house style,
    with measured receipts per phase and explicit non-claims.
  - docs/evidence/compat-g4/: README, receipt, scanner, commands, sums.
  - ROADMAP.md ledger row + shipped 0062 queue entry; docs/STATUS.md G4
    paragraph; CHANGELOG entry.
  - NOTICE.md now matches the tree: Apache-2.0 at the root, MIT for
    firmware/ only (the old text asked for a license that already exists).
  - PROJECT_ANALYSIS.md regenerated for this HEAD (48 src files, ~15.8k
    lines) instead of the 33e2c5c era.
  - src/cpu.h: the merged kgs_base/XMM comment is split, and the K6 SMP
    invariant is documented -- cpu_step() must be handed m->cpu, the
    current context, because its helpers read m->cpu directly.

Not established: no pinned-image BIOS-to-kernel boot, no shell
acceptance, no E820/boot_info_t agreement, no SMP/IOAPIC claim.  G3
remains open (the authoritative ISO still carries the original Stage 2);
G5-G6 stay planned.
